Take the FIRST Exif item in the file instead of the one describing the primary image.

A HEIC with two images carries two Exif items, and only the `cdsc` reference in `iref` says which
belongs to which. The failure this control proves a test can see is silent and wrong rather than
absent — the memo is dated from the decoy item, with no error anywhere — so the probe it must turn
red is the four-item fixture's capture date, and nothing else.

--- a/app/services/capture.py
+++ b/app/services/capture.py
@@ -362,8 +362,7 @@
     items = [item for item, kind in _heif_item_types(meta, start, end).items() if kind == b"Exif"]
     if not items:
         return None
-    if len(items) == 1:
-        return items[0]
+    return items[0]
     primary = _heif_primary_item(meta, start, end)
     iref = child(meta, start, end, b"iref")
     if primary is None or iref is None:
